-- title:
--   Admissible small constants over a valuation ring above q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime natural number with $q = 2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` such that $A$ lies over $q$ in the sense that the image of $q$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is a nonunit of $A$. Then there exist an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in $A$ such that, writing $A_0$ for the pullback $A \cap k_0$ of $A$ along the structure map $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$: $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$; $A_0$ is a henselian local ring; the residue field of $A_0$ is algebraically closed; and every $a \in A$ admits $c \in k_0$ with image in $A$ and $a - c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$. Moreover there exist a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ with image in $A$ together with a unit $u$ of $A$ satisfying $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   This provides the "small constants" package — a henselian discrete valuation subring $A_0$ of a subfield $k_0$ with algebraically closed residue field through which all residues of $A$ are represented, an auxiliary prime $\ell \ge 3$ coprime to $qM'$, a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity and a $(q^2-1)$-st root of $q$ up to a unit — in the case $q = 2$. It feeds the construction of supersingular regular prolongations and smooth-point charts on modular curves of full level at the prime $2$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_exists_admissible_smallConstants_of_eq_two.lean

